===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{gerund of|en|sink}}: the [[process#Noun|process]] by which something [[sink#Verb|sinks]], or is sunk.
#: {{usex|en|I witnessed the '''sinking''' of my ship from the shore.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1857|title=Pamphlets on Biology: Kofoid collection|passage=We must endeavour to realize a succession of gradual '''sinkings''' or depressions into deep water, alternating with gradual emergings into shallows, and eventually a gradual continued lifting of the whole district{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 August 10|title=Network News: New maintenance tunnel at Euston|journal=RAIL|issue=963|page=21|text=The excavation took 16 months of 24-hour working to complete and required the '''sinking''' of a 65ft shaft, from where workers carved out the passageway and lined it with reinforced steel and sprayed concrete.}}

